* How to Set Up the AFP
IsaFoR is based on the archive of formal proofs (AFP). The following local
setup is necessary:

  - initial steps when working on a stable version of the AFP

    1) Download and unpack the AFP corresponding to the version of Isabelle you
    are using from
      
      https://www.isa-afp.org/

  - initial steps when working on the development version of the AFP

    1) Create a local clone of the AFP via

      hg clone ssh://colo2-c703.uibk.ac.at//mercurial/afp

    (Note that this is just an intermediate clone of the real AFP for IsaFoR,
    which will be synchronized with the real AFP regularly.)

  - common steps

    2) In your $ISABELLE_HOME_USER/etc/settings add
    init_component "<path to local copy of AFP>"

    3) Create the heap image HOL-AFP via

      isabelle build -d '$ISAFOR' -b HOL-AFP

    4) Base your IsaFoR developments on the heap image HOL-AFP.

